## RPM Commands

```bash
# Install a local .rpm file
sudo rpm -i /home/bob/firefox-140.8.0.el9.x86_64.rpm

# Check if a package is installed
rpm -qa | grep wget

# Check with case insensitive search
rpm -qa | grep -i wget

# Get info about an installed package
rpm -qi firefox

# Remove a package
rpm -e firefox
```

RPM flags:

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-i` | Install |
| `-q` | Query |
| `-a` | All packages |
| `-e` | Erase/Remove |
| `-i` with `-q` | Info about package |

> 💡 `-qa` = query all installed packages
> 💡 Always use `grep -i` for case insensitive search

