## What is `yum provides`?

In Linux every command comes from a package. Sometimes the command name and package name are different.

| Command | Package it comes from |
|---------|----------------------|
| `tcpdump` | `tcpdump` |
| `ifconfig` | `net-tools` |
| `python3` | `python3` |
| `git` | `git` |

```bash
# Find which package provides a command
yum provides tcpdump

# Output:
# tcpdump-4.99.0-6.el9.x86_64
# Repo: baseos
```

> 💡 Use `yum provides` when you get `command not found` error
> 💡 It tells you exactly which package to install to get that command

