## Counting with wc -l

`wc` = Word Count command — but it counts more than just words.

| Command | What it counts |
|---------|---------------|
| `wc -l` | Number of lines |
| `wc -w` | Number of words |
| `wc -c` | Number of characters |

```bash
# Count number of repos
yum repolist | wc -l

# Count accurately (skip header line)
yum repolist | tail -n +2 | wc -l

# Count files in a directory
ls | wc -l

# Count running processes
ps aux | wc -l
```

> 💡 `wc -l` is the most used flag in DevOps
> 💡 Whenever you need to count anything — pipe it to `wc -l`

